
# HG changeset patch
# User Welpy-cw <58345540+Welpy-cw@users.noreply.github.com>
# Date 1790589050 -7200
# Node ID 94f5757f9c233999c0ae346e7c02f88c60f89d3c
# Parent  cab46a0fa6edca424a69183df198da4209fafa7b
Bug 2075316 - Show the To: field in Gloda search results. r=mkmelin

The To: field of messages shown in the Gloda (search) results view was
empty.

Bug 1935334 replaced the recipient loop with an Intl.ListFormat based
version, but read the display name from the wrong property. Gloda identity
objects expose the name as recipient.contact.name, not recipient.name, so
every name resolved to undefined and was dropped by filter(Boolean),
leaving only the "to:" label behind.

Render the names from recipient.contact?.name. The same rewrite had two
further problems: contactNames was sliced to MAX_RECIPIENTS - 1 before
being compared against MAX_RECIPIENTS, so the "N others" branch was
unreachable, and separator/recipient styling alternated via a boolean
rather than following part.type. Classify each node by part.type instead,
which is clearer than tracking position.

Count the "N others" from the number of recipients that were not shown,
rather than from a fixed MAX_RECIPIENTS offset, so that the names on
screen plus the label always add up to the total number of recipients.
This matters for recipients without a display name: they are not shown,
but they must still be counted, or a named recipient gets pushed out of
the visible slots while the label claims it was not.

Adds browser_glodaFacetResultMessage.js covering one, two, exactly three
and more than three recipients, the singular "1 other" form, recipients
without a name, the separator nodes produced by Intl.ListFormat, and the
To: label.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329240


